# Docker Development Commands

Use the same `--env-file` and Compose files for every command.

```bash
# Validate
docker compose --env-file .env.docker config --quiet

# Build and start
docker compose --env-file .env.docker build
docker compose --env-file .env.docker up -d --wait

# Inspect
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs --tail=150
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs -f app

# Run a non-destructive app command
docker compose --env-file .env.docker exec app <command>

# Stop containers while preserving named volumes
docker compose --env-file .env.docker down
```

Run migrations, seeds, imports, updates, and volume deletion only when their data effects are understood and explicitly intended. Do not place secret values directly on command lines or in this document.
